01:27:36.400 --> 01:27:39.800
Lauren Infantino: A bandpass filter will take a lower cutoff.

501
01:27:39.920 --> 01:27:45.389
Lauren Infantino: and a higher cutoff, and pass only the frequencies within the middle of that range.

502
01:27:45.750 --> 01:27:55.320
Lauren Infantino: and then a notch filter will do the exact opposite. You'll take a low cutoff and a high cutoff, and extract the frequencies in the middle and take them out.

503
01:27:56.340 --> 01:28:08.630
Lauren Infantino: So, for example, on this one in panel C, we have a fast Fourier transformation with a 50 Hertz interference, which is that narrow band noise from AC circuits and stuff.

